WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:04.620
To us regular people, landing a gig on an
immensely popular television series might

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:07.560
seem like the best work ever for an actor.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.100
Years and years of steady salary plus celebrity
status?

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.650
What could go wrong?

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:15.509
Well, sometimes those roles aren't quite all
they're cracked up to be.

00:00:15.509 --> 00:00:20.750
These actors hit it so big with these TV shows
that their careers still haven't fully recovered.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.330
Sarah Michelle Gellar

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:26.610
If you have to go down in history for one
role and one role only, it doesn't get much

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:31.910
better than being remembered as the kickass
Buffy Summers, the Slayer, the Chosen One.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:36.160
Buffy the Vampire Slayer was one of the most
influential television series to ever grace

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.410
the small screen, and fans have stuck by the
series for 20 years now.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:44.060
Sarah Michelle Gellar had a number of hits
during the Buffy years, like I Know What You

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.420
Did Last Summer and Cruel Intentions.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:52.180
But the post-Buffy years haven't been exactly
kind to Gellar, at least in a cinematic sense.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.740
Fortunately, her other pursuits have taken
off.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:01:00.090
In 2002 she married Freddie Prinze Jr., and
the two '90s sweethearts now have two children.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:06.170
In 2015, Gellar launched Foodstirs, a monthly
subscription service offering baking boxes.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:10.150
And in February 2017, she published her first
cookbook.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.440
Not bad for a former slayer...

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.030
David Schwimmer

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:19.150
Since his ten years as Ross Geller on Friends,
Schwimmer's career has basically slowed to

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:20.229
a halt.

00:01:20.229 --> 00:01:24.520
It's a typical case of a great television
role ruining an actor's chances for success

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:26.050
in other arenas.

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:30.490
Schwimmer himself even acknowledges the damage
his Friends success did to his career.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:35.700
In August 2016, he told The Hollywood Reporter
how his sudden celebrity status affected him:

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:39.670
"It made me want to hide under a baseball
cap and not be seen.

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:45.870
And I realized that after a while I was no
longer watching people; I was trying to hide."

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:50.460
And as if that weren't bad enough, Schwimmer's
enormous celebrity nearly destroyed his personal

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:51.460
life, too.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:57.930
"It messed with my relationship to other people
in a way that took years, I think, for me

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:01.990
to kind of adjust to and be comfortable with."

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:03.970
But there's hope on the horizon.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:08.240
More recently, Friends fans delighted in the
return of David Schwimmer as attorney Robert

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:12.840
Kardashian in the critically acclaimed FX
series The People vs. O.J. Simpson.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:17.250
And if that doesn't reboot his career, we
can always look forward to another Madagascar,

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:18.489
right?

00:02:18.489 --> 00:02:20.159
Sarah Jessica Parker

00:02:20.159 --> 00:02:23.810
Despite the fact that Sarah Jessica Parker
said that she would never do a television

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:29.450
series again after Sex and the City, she popped
up on HBO's Divorce, which has received mixed

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.769
reviews since its premiere in 2016.

00:02:31.769 --> 00:02:37.069
SJP had quite the career before Sex and the
City, beginning as a theater actor on Broadway,

00:02:37.069 --> 00:02:42.230
and going on to star in such films as L.A.
Story, Honeymoon in Vegas, Ed Wood, and Mars

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:43.230
Attacks!.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:48.950
But it still feels a little like SJP will
always be remembered as C-C-C-Carrie Bradshaw.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:52.890
And there's really nothing wrong with that
— Sex and the City has a pretty amazing

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:53.890
legacy.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:58.010
Just, please, don't make any more Sex and
the City movies.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.699
Jason Alexander

00:02:59.699 --> 00:03:04.730
From the cast of Seinfeld, there's Jerry,
Julia Louis-Dreyfus, and Michael Richards.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:07.209
We all know what happened to Michael Richards.

00:03:07.209 --> 00:03:11.059
And Louis-Dreyfus has gone on to star in another
great show, Veep.

00:03:11.059 --> 00:03:13.299
Jerry is still Jerry-ing right along.

00:03:13.299 --> 00:03:18.480
That leaves Jason Alexander, a fantastic comedic
actor...whose career just took a nosedive

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.870
after Seinfeld wrapped in 1998.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:23.290
So what has Alexander been up to since Seinfeld?

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:28.900
Well, aside from those KFC commercials, apparently
he's been playing a lot of poker, including

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:32.510
in televised tournaments where he donates
his winnings to charity.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:36.019
That's a big change from George Costanza,
but hey, good for him!

00:03:36.019 --> 00:03:38.069
The crew of the Enterprise

00:03:38.069 --> 00:03:42.260
Although Shakespearean-trained actor Patrick
Stewart has gone on to many more major roles

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:47.340
in his long and prolific career after playing
Captain Jean-Luc Picard, the rest of the Star

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:50.189
Trek: The Next Generation cast was not so
lucky.

00:03:50.189 --> 00:03:55.370
Jonathan Frakes, LeVar Burton, and Brent Spiner
have all failed to embark on major careers

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:56.559
post-Trek.

00:03:56.559 --> 00:04:01.319
That speaks more to the career stifling effects
of the iconic characters they played, rather

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.160
than their talents as actors.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:03.680
"Hey, Troy?"

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:07.180
"Hi, I'm LeVar Burton!"

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:15.370
Still, the Star Trek fanbase is a die-hard,
dedicated, uh, enterprise.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:20.790
Let's hope the Star Trek legacy has been enough
to sustain these three over the years.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:21.880
Jon Hamm

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:27.820
Mad Men's Jon Hamm is so totally Don Draper
that the only parts he's had since are simply

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:32.780
different versions of that same character
— like his brief cameo in Bridesmaids or

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.390
his role in 30 Rock.

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:37.050
"I guess I'll see you around then…"

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:38.100
"Or as the French say…"

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.080
"Yeah."

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:47.070
But the fact remains that since Mad Men wrapped
in 2015, Jon Hamm's career has been mostly

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:49.430
dormant … or just flying under the radar.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:53.680
It's only been two years, so let's hope that
Hamm will be able to find a role that gives

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.080
him a break from the Don Draper persona.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:01.850
So far — unless you count corny tax-preparation
commercials — it hasn't happened.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:03.140
Lauren Ambrose

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:05.400
Lauren Ambrose: What happened?

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.400
We miss you.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:10.720
Ambrose is best remembered for her turn as
Claire on HBO's Six Feet Under, one of the

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:13.880
most relatable and beloved characters of the
series.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:18.510
Before that, you may have seen Ambrose trapped
in a bathroom with Seth Green in 1998's Can't

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:19.510
Hardly Wait.

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:25.300
But after Six Feet Under ended in 2005, Ambrose
hasn't gotten many shots in big-name productions,

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.210
aside from a supporting role in The X-Files
reboot.

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:29.890
We'd love to see her again!

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:31.770
Hopefully we'll get our wish soon...

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:33.300
Thanks for watching!

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:36.050
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:38.000
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

